        "/api/v1/webhooks/pagopar": {
            "post": {
                "operationId": "v1_webhooks_pagopar_create",
                "description": "`POST /api/v1/webhooks/pagopar` (spec: payment-processing, \"Webhook Idempotency\").\n\nUnauthenticated by API key — Pagopar does not hold one of our keys.\nAuthenticity instead rests entirely on `PaymentGateway.verify_webhook`'s\ngateway-signature check (see `adapters/pagopar/signature.py`'s loud\nUNCONFIRMED-algorithm warning, and its fail-closed behavior when\n`PAGOPAR_PRIVATE_KEY` is unset).\n\nDesign §5 layered security, items (3)-(5) implemented here:\npersist `WebhookEvent` BEFORE any state change (even for a payload that\nfails signature verification, for forensics), and rely on the\n`(gateway, event_id)` unique constraint as the idempotency gate — an\n`IntegrityError` means \"already processed\", answered with 200 and no\nside effects rather than an error (spec: \"Duplicate/replayed callback\").",
                "tags": [
                    "v1"
                ],
                "security": [
                    {}
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "No response body"
                    }
                }
            }
        }
